WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.940
Treasure Island

00:00:06.230 --> 00:00:07.860
But it exists, Jim.

00:00:09.110 --> 00:00:14.070
One day, I hope to discover
what matters most to me.

00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:15.790
I'm sure it exists.

00:00:19.390 --> 00:00:20.700
If it doesn't...

00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:27.090
If it doesn't,

00:00:27.090 --> 00:00:29.670
it would all be too sad.

00:00:35.190 --> 00:00:36.550
<i>Silver had disappeared.</i>

00:00:37.030 --> 00:00:39.560
Silver! Silver!

00:00:42.470 --> 00:00:46.070
<i>He returned to the Hispaniola to take "his share".</i>

00:00:46.070 --> 00:00:47.690
<i>What a brilliant exit.</i>

00:00:48.470 --> 00:00:49.570
Silver!

00:00:50.670 --> 00:00:54.990
<i>Without even saying goodbye to me, he disappeared.</i>

00:00:57.370 --> 00:01:00.930
Treasure
Island

00:00:57.370 --> 00:01:00.730
Takarajima

00:01:07.210 --> 00:01:09.540
saa ikou

00:01:07.210 --> 00:01:09.540
Come, let's go

00:01:09.790 --> 00:01:12.630
yume ni mita shima heto

00:01:09.790 --> 00:01:12.630
To the island that I've dreamed of

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:16.470
nami wo koete kaze ni notte

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:16.470
Across the waves, on the wind

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:19.350
umi hedeyou

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:19.350
We'll travel the oceans

00:01:19.760 --> 00:01:22.270
ikute ni wa

00:01:19.760 --> 00:01:22.270
Many of us

00:01:22.520 --> 00:01:25.270
minna mada shiranai

00:01:22.520 --> 00:01:25.270
Still don't know of

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:29.020
fushigi na hiru to yoru toga

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:29.020
The days and nights full of mystery

00:01:29.270 --> 00:01:31.520
matte iru darou

00:01:29.270 --> 00:01:31.520
That await us there

00:01:31.770 --> 00:01:35.030
itsumo shinji you

00:01:31.770 --> 00:01:35.030
We must always have trust

00:01:35.650 --> 00:01:38.280
magokoro wo

00:01:35.650 --> 00:01:38.280
And be sincere

00:01:38.780 --> 00:01:44.540
yuuki wo mune ni susumou yo

00:01:38.780 --> 00:01:44.540
And have courage in our hearts to move forward

00:01:44.830 --> 00:01:47.670
tade hitotsu no

00:01:44.830 --> 00:01:47.670
I only...

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:51.090
akogare dake wa

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:51.090
...have one desire

00:01:51.340 --> 00:01:53.380
doko no dare ni mo

00:01:51.340 --> 00:01:53.380
And no one...

00:01:53.710 --> 00:02:00.090
kese wa shinai sa

00:01:53.710 --> 00:02:00.090
...will ever take it away

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:06.640
tade hitotsu no

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:06.640
I only...

00:02:06.890 --> 00:02:09.940
akogare dake wa

00:02:06.890 --> 00:02:09.940
...have one desire

00:02:10.190 --> 00:02:12.270
doko no dare ni mo

00:02:10.190 --> 00:02:12.270
And no one...

00:02:12.570 --> 00:02:19.200
kese wa shinai sa

00:02:12.570 --> 00:02:19.200
...will ever take it away

00:02:25.670 --> 00:02:30.460
episode

00:02:25.670 --> 00:02:30.460
Flint Can't Fly Anymore

00:02:37.150 --> 00:02:39.010
Madam, there's a letter for you!

00:02:39.790 --> 00:02:41.970
I believe it's from Jim.

00:02:42.310 --> 00:02:43.950
Thank you for your trouble.

00:02:43.950 --> 00:02:46.430
Don't be, it's nothing.
Goodbye.

00:02:56.630 --> 00:03:01.320
"Mother, I'm writing this letter to you from a Bristol Hotel."

00:03:02.150 --> 00:03:06.420
<i>"Mother, this letter allows me to tell you
of my approaching return."</i>

00:03:07.290 --> 00:03:11.190
<i>"That said, I still have to leave Bristol and get back to Black Hill,</i>

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:13.950
<i>so it'll take about four or five days."</i>

00:03:13.950 --> 00:03:17.210
<i>"I wish you could've seen the crowd that was waiting for us."</i>

00:03:17.630 --> 00:03:21.680
<i>"Our Hispaniola arrived in Bristol's port under loud cheering."</i>

00:03:23.550 --> 00:03:26.110
<i>"The news of the treasure's discovery...</i>

00:03:26.110 --> 00:03:29.060
<i>...must have made it to England. Hence the welcome."</i>

00:03:30.030 --> 00:03:33.230
<i>"Even the Royal Guard was there to welcome us."</i>

00:03:35.790 --> 00:03:37.940
<i>"We were welcomed like true heroes."</i>

00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:43.560
<i>"All the country's newspapers told of
our stories and requested interviews,</i>

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:47.870
<i>but our fight against the pirates is a painful memory."</i>

00:03:50.540 --> 00:03:54.380
<i>"We had to take a room in the Bristol Hotel...</i>

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:57.800
<i>...to await the decision made by The Crown and authorities."</i>

00:03:58.390 --> 00:04:03.950
<i>"So you see, Mother, since Black Hill is only a day's carriage ride away,</i>

00:04:03.950 --> 00:04:06.140
<i>I wanted to write you this letter."</i>

00:04:06.950 --> 00:04:08.560
Madam!

00:04:12.470 --> 00:04:15.480
Tell me, is it true that you have news of Jim?

00:04:16.510 --> 00:04:20.570
"PS: before I forget,
say hello to Lilly for me."

00:04:21.140 --> 00:04:24.790
What, "Before I forget"?
That's not very nice!

00:04:28.310 --> 00:04:32.160
Say, madam. What if we went to Bristol to look for Jim?

00:04:33.030 --> 00:04:36.380
We shouldn't... Every ship needs a port to return home to.

00:04:36.870 --> 00:04:39.830
When it comes to her husband or son,

00:04:39.830 --> 00:04:43.670
she knows to have faith and wait patiently.

00:04:43.670 --> 00:04:48.780
Lily, when you have a nice husband and children, you'll understand.

00:04:49.290 --> 00:04:51.520
I-I already do, madam.

00:04:58.270 --> 00:05:00.110
Has The Crown made its decision?

00:05:00.110 --> 00:05:03.030
Yes, we were awarded the Order of Merit.

00:05:03.030 --> 00:05:05.680
Have you been entitled to a share of the treasure?

00:05:05.680 --> 00:05:08.790
Each of us received 1000 pounds.

00:05:09.150 --> 00:05:12.720
Captain, tell us about a difficult part of the journey.

00:05:12.720 --> 00:05:15.710
A sailor's life is difficult every day.
Picking one is impossible!

00:05:16.590 --> 00:05:21.060
You're the youngest, but you seem to have fought bravely, didn't you?

00:05:21.870 --> 00:05:23.430
Were you ever afraid?

00:05:25.110 --> 00:05:26.640
How will you spend the money?

00:05:26.640 --> 00:05:27.720
That's easy.

00:05:27.720 --> 00:05:32.050
I want a farm. With horses, workers and booze from around the world.

00:05:32.060 --> 00:05:34.910
Come on!
1000 pounds isn't enough.

00:05:34.910 --> 00:05:38.270
What? Prices have risen that much in ten years?

00:05:38.600 --> 00:05:41.770
Captain Smollett and Dr. Livesey
gave the orders.

00:05:47.150 --> 00:05:47.860
<i>Gray?</i>

00:05:58.430 --> 00:05:59.860
Where are you going, Gray?

00:06:02.350 --> 00:06:05.680
This bustle is wearing me out.
I'm going back to Ireland.

00:06:06.310 --> 00:06:07.180
To Ireland?

00:06:07.710 --> 00:06:09.950
Yes.
That's where I'm from.

00:06:09.950 --> 00:06:12.830
Say goodbye to everyone for me, Jim.

00:06:12.830 --> 00:06:14.180
Wait, I'll see you off!

00:06:20.070 --> 00:06:22.530
What luck they have.
They're so happy.

00:06:22.530 --> 00:06:25.690
They've been awarded.
And given 1000 pounds...

00:06:26.590 --> 00:06:30.370
Yet gain, Puppy the Seagull was unable to fly.

00:06:32.250 --> 00:06:35.430
What am I going to say to my nine brothers?

00:06:36.030 --> 00:06:36.660
Gray...

00:06:37.960 --> 00:06:38.870
Hold out your hands, Puppy.

00:06:43.020 --> 00:06:45.750
That must be 500 pounds,
give or take.

00:06:45.750 --> 00:06:46.920
Your share.

00:06:48.320 --> 00:06:49.510
Gray...

00:06:49.510 --> 00:06:53.550
It's nothing. Silver would've probably given you more.

00:06:57.230 --> 00:06:58.350
Goodbye.

00:06:58.950 --> 00:07:00.730
Gray, take care of yourself!

00:07:02.270 --> 00:07:04.700
We'll see each other again one day!

00:07:06.710 --> 00:07:08.400
Including Silver, of course!

00:07:10.710 --> 00:07:12.370
Yes, for sure!

00:07:15.870 --> 00:07:19.830
<i>Yes, I'm sure of it.
Silver will be there, too.</i>

00:07:23.990 --> 00:07:31.830
Fifteen men on a dead man's chest...

00:07:31.830 --> 00:07:37.190
Yo-ho-ho!
...and a bottle of rum!

00:07:37.190 --> 00:07:44.270
Drink and the devil had done for the rest...

00:07:44.270 --> 00:07:48.870
Yo-ho-ho!
...and another bottle of rum!

00:07:48.870 --> 00:07:53.980
Yo-ho-ho!
...and another bottle of rum!

00:08:12.170 --> 00:08:15.050
<i>We're home!</i>

00:08:19.830 --> 00:08:26.450
Fifteen men on a dead man's chest...

00:08:26.450 --> 00:08:30.780
Yo-ho-ho!
...and a bottle of rum!

00:08:55.830 --> 00:08:57.180
Father...

00:08:57.180 --> 00:09:00.580
I finally went out there, too.
To sea, that is.

00:09:08.220 --> 00:09:11.070
He's sleeping. You must be really worn out, huh Jim?

00:09:11.470 --> 00:09:14.470
I'm sure he's overworked himself.

00:09:14.470 --> 00:09:16.810
Men are hopeless, aren't they?

00:09:17.910 --> 00:09:20.950
Truly the son of his father.
Hard-working just like him.

00:09:40.910 --> 00:09:42.260
So this is THE map?

00:09:42.260 --> 00:09:42.810
Yep.

00:09:43.270 --> 00:09:47.640
Dr. Livesey and Mr. Trelawney left it to me as a souvenir.

00:09:47.640 --> 00:09:50.230
After all, it was me who found it.

00:09:51.030 --> 00:09:54.190
Actually, this map belonged to Billy Bones.

00:09:54.950 --> 00:09:57.700
If I had never met Billy Bones,

00:09:57.700 --> 00:10:02.660
there wouldn't have been a map or an adventure on Treasure Island.

00:10:06.670 --> 00:10:07.620
Billy Bones...

00:10:12.310 --> 00:10:14.380
I went to Treasure Island!

00:10:14.990 --> 00:10:18.190
<i>Look, mateys, it's over there.
On the other side of the sea.</i>

00:10:18.190 --> 00:10:19.490
<i>Do you see it, mateys?</i>

00:10:20.390 --> 00:10:21.140
<i>It's beautiful!</i>

00:10:22.830 --> 00:10:26.140
<i>Jim, give me one last glass of rum!</i>

00:10:37.490 --> 00:10:39.820
<i>I see, so you've finally returned, Jim?</i>

00:10:40.350 --> 00:10:42.190
<i>Yes, I've done it, Billy.</i>

00:10:42.190 --> 00:10:45.350
<i>I see, that's great.
And, what of the treasure?</i>

00:10:45.350 --> 00:10:46.370
<i>I found it!</i>

00:10:46.370 --> 00:10:50.390
<i>The sea, the adventure and everyone I met...</i>

00:10:50.390 --> 00:10:52.330
<i>That's my treasure!</i>

00:10:54.390 --> 00:10:55.810
<i>Look at you.</i>

00:10:55.810 --> 00:10:59.120
<i>Still a kid, but spoken like a true sailor.</i>

00:11:21.950 --> 00:11:24.310
Jim, what are you going to do now?

00:11:24.310 --> 00:11:26.370
Are you going out to sea like your father?

00:11:26.370 --> 00:11:29.120
Who knows. I can't tell
what the future holds.

00:11:31.030 --> 00:11:34.150
Come, let's go. Your mother is waiting for us with dinner.

00:11:34.150 --> 00:11:34.950
Okay.

00:11:34.950 --> 00:11:36.380
Come on, let's race!

00:11:36.380 --> 00:11:37.390
Okay!

00:11:39.390 --> 00:11:41.470
You can't tell what the future holds?

00:11:41.470 --> 00:11:45.260
But Jim, if you can't tell if you go out to sea, then who can?

00:12:04.070 --> 00:12:05.410
What is it, Jim?

00:12:05.410 --> 00:12:07.190
N-No, it's nothing.

00:12:07.190 --> 00:12:07.790
Let's go!

00:12:07.790 --> 00:12:08.490
Okay!

00:12:30.120 --> 00:12:32.730
<i>And so, ten years passed.</i>

00:12:44.320 --> 00:12:46.540
<i>For those who were part of the adventure on Treasure Island,</i>

00:12:46.540 --> 00:12:49.580
<i>those ten years have also passed.</i>

00:12:53.200 --> 00:12:58.500
<i>Puppy is currently in London where he opened a hardware store, "The Seagull".</i>

00:12:59.200 --> 00:13:02.200
<i>He opened stores for each of his brothers...</i>

00:13:02.200 --> 00:13:04.870
<i>...and the chain "The Seagull" became a great success.</i>

00:13:08.000 --> 00:13:09.000
<i>As for Ben Gunn...</i>

00:13:09.600 --> 00:13:10.560
<i>Indeed.</i>

00:13:10.560 --> 00:13:15.690
<i>After being abandoned by Flint, he spent ten years alone on the island. That Ben Gunn.</i>

00:13:16.280 --> 00:13:20.880
<i>Three weeks was enough for him to spend all of his 1000 pounds.</i>

00:13:20.880 --> 00:13:24.650
<i>It disappeared in glasses of rum and short-lived luxury.</i>

00:13:25.070 --> 00:13:28.560
<i>However, he is now a lock keeper in the country...</i>

00:13:28.560 --> 00:13:30.620
<i>...and all the children adore him.</i>

00:13:37.080 --> 00:13:40.260
<i>Hunter got married and has four children.</i>

00:13:40.930 --> 00:13:45.470
<i>He has a farm on the heights of Side-Saddle, near Black Hill.</i>

00:13:46.080 --> 00:13:48.430
<i>Captain Smollett navigates the Indian Ocean.</i>

00:13:48.840 --> 00:13:51.080
<i>Refusing to talk about retirement,</i>

00:13:51.080 --> 00:13:53.390
<i>he still paces the decks of ships.</i>

00:14:00.340 --> 00:14:01.390
<i>And...</i>

00:14:02.670 --> 00:14:04.330
<i>Gray died five years ago.</i>

00:14:15.620 --> 00:14:19.420
<i>He gave his money to an independent movement of Ireland.</i>

00:14:21.040 --> 00:14:24.670
<i>He even took part in desperate
combat against the regular army.</i>

00:14:29.430 --> 00:14:32.030
<i>Eventually, he died courageously.</i>

00:14:37.380 --> 00:14:39.060
S-Silver...

00:14:39.060 --> 00:14:41.990
How would you get out of this situation?

00:14:53.190 --> 00:14:54.790
<i>Regarding Gray and Silver...</i>

00:14:54.790 --> 00:14:56.610
<i>They spent their time quarreling,</i>

00:14:56.610 --> 00:14:59.280
<i>but it's possible that out of all of us,</i>

00:14:59.280 --> 00:15:00.790
<i>Gray understood Silver best.</i>

00:15:03.490 --> 00:15:07.010
<i>For better or worse, ten years have passed since our return from Treasure Island.</i>

00:15:18.080 --> 00:15:20.190
Okay, here it is.

00:15:20.840 --> 00:15:22.900
Here's the document in question.

00:15:24.040 --> 00:15:26.280
Another story about a map, Trelawney?

00:15:26.280 --> 00:15:28.280
It's authentic, this time.

00:15:28.760 --> 00:15:31.320
Most likely the treasure of Captain Kidd.

00:15:31.320 --> 00:15:36.550
Anyways, it's rumoured that this island of Jipang is covered with gold.

00:15:37.160 --> 00:15:40.930
Let's go, my friend, Livesey.
We must go at all costs!

00:15:43.640 --> 00:15:46.680
Yes, but...
This time, Silver isn't here.

00:15:46.680 --> 00:15:49.970
Silver...
Yes, that's true, Silver isn't here.

00:15:49.970 --> 00:15:54.600
Silver... Back then, he sent chills down my spine,

00:15:54.600 --> 00:15:58.120
but without him we would've never had such an adventure.

00:15:58.120 --> 00:16:01.560
Yes, but what's become of him?
Do you have any news?

00:16:01.560 --> 00:16:03.760
No, not a word.

00:16:03.760 --> 00:16:05.650
Yes, you may enter.
It's open.

00:16:07.290 --> 00:16:09.110
It's been a long time.

00:16:09.110 --> 00:16:11.570
Mr. Trelawney, Dr. Livesey.

00:16:12.720 --> 00:16:14.280
Who might you be?

00:16:14.800 --> 00:16:16.540
Come on, it's me.
Me!

00:16:16.540 --> 00:16:19.120
Oh, Jim!
Jim Hawkins!

00:16:19.620 --> 00:16:22.300
What a surprise.
When did you get back?

00:16:22.300 --> 00:16:25.080
You've been at sea for a very long time.

00:16:25.080 --> 00:16:28.090
Yes, ten years.
I returned this morning.

00:16:29.360 --> 00:16:30.760
Yes, I see now.

00:16:30.760 --> 00:16:33.510
I almost had a heart attack.

00:16:34.600 --> 00:16:35.970
Why's that?

00:16:35.970 --> 00:16:38.050
Because of Silver!
I thought you were Silver!

00:16:38.050 --> 00:16:42.980
You've grown so much.
For a moment, I thought you were him.

00:16:44.400 --> 00:16:45.440
Really?

00:16:47.600 --> 00:16:50.400
You've really grown, too, Benbow.

00:16:50.400 --> 00:16:53.470
Now no one can mistake you for a cat.

00:16:54.730 --> 00:16:56.370
S-Stop it, Benbow.

00:17:02.240 --> 00:17:05.400
By the way, Jim.
How many voyages have you made?

00:17:05.400 --> 00:17:08.250
Yes, if I count the very short ones, fifteen.

00:17:08.250 --> 00:17:13.220
Geez, you've spent your life at sea. I know someone who may have had enough.

00:17:14.420 --> 00:17:16.700
Don't play innocent.
I'm talking about Lilly.

00:17:16.700 --> 00:17:18.890
When are you going to marry her?

00:17:19.400 --> 00:17:21.770
W-Well...
Y-Yes, I...

00:17:21.770 --> 00:17:23.580
You haven't decided yet?

00:17:23.580 --> 00:17:26.730
Really, a sailor's idiocy is incurable.

00:17:27.440 --> 00:17:30.690
That's rich!
Well said, I commend you.

00:17:44.080 --> 00:17:45.630
I've made you wait, Lilly.

00:17:46.320 --> 00:17:46.840
For you.

00:17:48.200 --> 00:17:50.750
I bought this coral ring on my voyage.

00:17:53.800 --> 00:17:54.810
Here.

00:18:02.120 --> 00:18:03.640
The sea will be our chapel.

00:18:07.310 --> 00:18:08.840
You know...

00:18:08.840 --> 00:18:12.270
I couldn't tell Dr. Livesey and Mr. Trelawney, after all.

00:18:12.600 --> 00:18:15.650
A month ago, I ran into Silver.

00:18:17.560 --> 00:18:20.740
It was in a small port of North Africa.

00:18:26.430 --> 00:18:29.420
A glass of rum and some milk for him.

00:18:31.710 --> 00:18:33.910
So you're the one everyone's talking about?

00:18:33.910 --> 00:18:36.130
"Jim the sailor and his leopard."

00:18:36.470 --> 00:18:39.830
You have the reputation of being a great dog of the sea.

00:18:39.830 --> 00:18:41.040
Please stop it.

00:18:41.040 --> 00:18:42.520
You make me sound like a pirate.

00:18:43.910 --> 00:18:46.060
I'm a respectable chief petty officer.

00:18:46.710 --> 00:18:48.820
I don't like the rumours very much.

00:18:49.520 --> 00:18:53.290
Come on, bet on a glass of rum with me!

00:18:56.230 --> 00:18:58.470
It's just one glass.
Whether you win or lose.

00:18:58.470 --> 00:19:01.070
E-Even so... Arm-wrestling isn't really my thing.

00:19:01.470 --> 00:19:03.870
Don't be stingy.
It just depends on luck.

00:19:03.870 --> 00:19:07.500
N-No, I can't. The other day, it cost me five glasses.

00:19:08.370 --> 00:19:10.390
You're young, but you're a real wuss.

00:19:10.390 --> 00:19:13.960
Hey, is there anyone who wants to challenge me at arm-wrestling?

00:19:25.470 --> 00:19:28.890
You'll do just fine.
We have a game, young man?

00:19:30.850 --> 00:19:33.510
Win or lose, it's just one glass.

00:19:33.510 --> 00:19:34.820
There's no tricks.

00:19:35.950 --> 00:19:37.610
Very well, I accept.

00:19:42.490 --> 00:19:44.450
So young man, shall we start?

00:20:21.350 --> 00:20:25.320
Thanks, it's been a while since I had good booze. Farewell.

00:20:28.430 --> 00:20:30.410
Silver!
Don't you recognize me?

00:20:32.330 --> 00:20:35.310
It's me! Look!
It's Jim Hawkins!

00:20:35.310 --> 00:20:38.250
I wanted to see you...
I really wanted to see you again!

00:20:38.250 --> 00:20:40.210
Jim Hawkins?

00:20:40.210 --> 00:20:42.290
Yes, it's been ten years!

00:20:42.290 --> 00:20:45.460
Ten years?
Sorry, I don't remember.

00:20:46.180 --> 00:20:51.780
Young'un, don't take it personally, but reliving old memories spoils the taste of rum.

00:20:57.520 --> 00:21:00.230
He reminds me somewhat of
this man who, six months ago,

00:21:00.230 --> 00:21:02.240
lost the wife he shared his life with.

00:21:02.240 --> 00:21:03.490
Or so someone told me...

00:21:10.510 --> 00:21:12.200
Silver! Silver!

00:21:13.790 --> 00:21:15.330
Silver! Silver!

00:21:16.830 --> 00:21:18.250
You didn't see him again?

00:21:20.670 --> 00:21:21.960
No, I saw him.

00:21:22.750 --> 00:21:26.340
Then and there, I saw the Silver I admired.

00:21:32.830 --> 00:21:35.770
What's wrong with you, Flint?

00:21:36.350 --> 00:21:39.730
You're not old enough yet to stop flying.

00:21:39.730 --> 00:21:44.190
Come on, Flint, fly.
Your wings are still strong.

00:21:44.190 --> 00:21:48.350
Go on, be strong, Flint.
You can still fly.

00:21:48.350 --> 00:21:51.350
Come on, Flint.
Look, I'm strong too.

00:21:51.350 --> 00:21:54.040
You saw that bit of wrestling, eh?

00:21:57.990 --> 00:22:01.020
You see?
You can still fly, Flint.

00:22:02.830 --> 00:22:05.010
Good.
Let's go, Flint.

00:22:05.830 --> 00:22:08.960
Wherever we go...
whatever the dangers...

00:22:08.960 --> 00:22:12.620
If we want it, our wings will carry us!

00:22:24.980 --> 00:22:26.320
<i>I once knew him.</i>

00:22:26.320 --> 00:22:27.740
<i>I really did.</i>

00:22:27.740 --> 00:22:29.200
<i>My...</i>

00:22:27.890 --> 00:22:32.750
The   End

00:22:29.200 --> 00:22:30.810
<i>My friend Silver!</i>

00:22:33.670 --> 00:22:38.710
shiokaze yo omae mo

00:22:33.670 --> 00:22:38.710
Hey sea breeze

00:22:38.710 --> 00:22:44.520
tomodachi naraba tsutaete

00:22:38.710 --> 00:22:44.520
If you're my friend then carry

00:22:45.740 --> 00:22:50.730
furusato ni nokoshite kita

00:22:45.740 --> 00:22:50.730
To my home that I've left behind

00:22:50.730 --> 00:22:56.170
natsukashii haha ni hitokoto

00:22:50.730 --> 00:22:56.170
A word to my dear mother

00:22:56.170 --> 00:23:01.580
boku wa genki de yattemasu

00:22:56.170 --> 00:23:01.580
Tell her that I'm doing fine

00:23:01.580 --> 00:23:07.040
kaban ippai no

00:23:01.580 --> 00:23:07.040
And that my bag filled

00:23:07.040 --> 00:23:12.670
nozomi to yume to takaramono

00:23:07.040 --> 00:23:12.670
With hopes, dreams and treasures

00:23:12.670 --> 00:23:18.530
kakaete kaeritai

00:23:12.670 --> 00:23:18.530
Will be brought back

00:23:19.620 --> 00:23:25.120
yuuyake wo senaka ni

00:23:19.620 --> 00:23:25.120
The sunset on my back

00:23:25.120 --> 00:23:31.010
kamome wo kata ni tomarasete

00:23:25.120 --> 00:23:31.010
And a seagull perched on my shoulder

00:23:31.010 --> 00:23:40.730
boku wa fukimasu kuchibue wo

00:23:31.010 --> 00:23:40.730
I blow out a whistle
